Which solid does this net make?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (1.2,2); \draw (1.2,0) rectangle (2.4,2); \draw (2.4,0) rectangle (3.6,2);
\draw (1.2,2)--(1.8,3.2)--(2.4,2)--cycle; \draw (1.2,0)--(1.8,-1.2)--(2.4,0)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What solid does this net make?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (2,2); \draw (0,0)--(1,-1.5)--(2,0)--cycle; \draw (2,0)--(3.5,1)--(2,2)--cycle; \draw (2,2)--(1,3.7)--(0,2)--cycle; \draw (0,2)--(-1.5,1)--(0,0)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Why is this not a cube net?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\foreach \x/\y in {-1/0,0/0,1/0,0/1,1/1,2/1}{\draw (\x,\y) rectangle ++(1,1);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
